    "title": "GCSC's Danna Aguilera enters the Commodore history book - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Karli Koskovich ,\n54 minutes ago\nPANAMA CITY, Fla ( WMBB ) – The Gulf Coast State volleyball team finished with a record of 32-5 and third in the NJCAA but sophomore pin hitter Danna Aguilera took it one step further and made history.\nAguilera cemented herself as one of the top volleyball players in the country, earning back-to-back NJCAA Division II First-Team All-American honors.\nThis year, she totaled 482 kills, boosting her to the 12th best in the nation. She also added 63 aces and more than 550 digs, pushing her to finish with 566 total points, ranking 10th in the country.\nAnd her impact is not just about this season.\nAguilera is already the Lady Commodores’ all-time leader in career kills with 873, and she sits second in program history with 951 career digs.\nShe also now owns two of the top single-season kill totals in school history.\nWith this year’s selection, Danna Aguilera has solidified her legacy as one of the best to ever wear a Lady Commodores jersey.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to mypanhandle.com.",
